86ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">rare pol=
itical climb-down</a><span> for a leader who has been in power for 12 years=
=2E The protesters went home, for a while at least. But, as Mujib writes, t=
hey were also emboldened.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georg=
ia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>India=E2=80=99s youth movement i=
s a headache for Modi, and he=E2=80=99s been struggling to find a workable =
playbook. Partly that=E2=80=99s because India has a lot of young people: mo=
re than 40 percent of India=E2=80=99s 1.4 billion people are under 25. And =
partly it=E2=80=99s because the youth movement has cut across traditional p=
olitical divides in India, making it much harder for Modi and his allies to=
 box in and demonize.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,s=
erif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=80=99s no coincidence that thi=
s movement first galvanized around the issue of dysfunction in India=E2=80=
